---
export const title = 'Other hierarchies';
export const order = 200;
import DemoComponentCard from '../../../../components/DemoComponentCard.astro';
---

<p>
  The chart works for any tree: taxonomies, sitemaps, decision trees, a bill of materials. <code>orientation="horizontal"</code>
  lays it out left to right, which suits deep trees with short labels. Give items an <code>icon</code> (and an
  <code>accent</code>) instead of an avatar.
</p>

<DemoComponentCard lang={'html'}>
  <wc-tree-chart id="sitemap" orientation="horizontal" style="height: 440px; width: 100%;">
    <wc-diagram-controls slot="controls"></wc-diagram-controls>
  </wc-tree-chart>

  <script is:inline>
    (() => {
      document.querySelector('#sitemap').items = [
        { id: 'home', headline: 'Home', icon: 'home' },
        { id: 'products', parentId: 'home', headline: 'Products', icon: 'inventory_2', accent: 'blue' },
        { id: 'pricing', parentId: 'home', headline: 'Pricing', icon: 'sell', accent: 'green' },
        { id: 'docs', parentId: 'home', headline: 'Docs', icon: 'menu_book', accent: 'purple' },
        { id: 'flow', parentId: 'products', headline: 'Workflows', supportingText: '/products/workflows', icon: 'account_tree', accent: 'blue' },
        { id: 'maps', parentId: 'products', headline: 'Service maps', supportingText: '/products/maps', icon: 'hub', accent: 'blue' },
        { id: 'start', parentId: 'docs', headline: 'Getting started', icon: 'rocket_launch', accent: 'purple' },
        { id: 'api', parentId: 'docs', headline: 'API reference', icon: 'code', accent: 'purple' },
      ];
    })();
  </script>
</DemoComponentCard>

<h3>Lazy loading</h3>
<p>
  Give an item <code>hasChildren</code> and add its children when it fires <code>expand</code>. Its chip shows a spinner
  until they arrive.
</p>

<DemoComponentCard lang={'html'}>
  <wc-tree-chart id="lazy" style="height: 420px; width: 100%;"></wc-tree-chart>

  <script is:inline>
    (() => {
      const chart = document.querySelector('#lazy');
      chart.items = [
        { id: 'all', headline: 'All departments', icon: 'corporate_fare' },
        { id: 'sales', parentId: 'all', headline: 'Sales', icon: 'trending_up', accent: 'green', hasChildren: true },
        { id: 'support', parentId: 'all', headline: 'Support', icon: 'support_agent', accent: 'orange', hasChildren: true },
      ];
      chart.addEventListener('expand', e => {
        const { id, item } = e.detail;
        if (!item.hasChildren) return;
        // Pretend to fetch the children.
        setTimeout(() => {
          chart.items = [
            ...chart.items.map(i => (i.id === id ? { ...i, hasChildren: false } : i)),
            ...[1, 2, 3].map(n => ({ id: `${id}-${n}`, parentId: id, headline: `${item.headline} team ${n}`, icon: 'groups', accent: item.accent })),
          ];
        }, 900);
      });
    })();
  </script>
</DemoComponentCard>

<h3>Keyboard</h3>
<p>
  The chart is one tab stop. In a vertical chart Up goes to the parent, Down to the first child, and Left and Right to
  siblings (mirrored in right-to-left pages); a horizontal chart turns the keys. Home and End go to the first and last
  item, <wc-kbd keys="*"></wc-kbd> expands all siblings, <wc-kbd keys="enter"></wc-kbd> selects and
  <wc-kbd keys="shift+enter"></wc-kbd> expands or collapses. The canvas keys of <code>wc-diagram</code> work too.
</p>
